<task id="112" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>UAT-R3 — render Compose AI action results as prose (per-action formatter) instead of a raw JSON fence</title>
    <phase>9 UAT-Fix</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>114</blocks>
    <tags>react,compose,frontend,ai,uat-remediation</tags>
    <rigor-hint reason="Modifies .tsx result-rendering path on the dispatch→chat seam; FULL; real-bus DoD">FULL</rigor-hint>
    <model-tier reason="Contained client formatter keyed on known output schemas; sonnet">sonnet</model-tier>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="Edits ConversationPane.tsx (dispatchComposeAction) + the formatter module (DocumentUploadedEventStream.ts / summarizeRouting.ts). Disjoint from 110 (BFF) and 111 (ComposeAiToolbar/ComposeEditor). NOTE: 113 also touches ConversationPane.tsx — 113 is Wave 2, so no co-run.">true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    UAT defect #3b/#3c: clicking an inline AI action shows a raw-JSON-looking blob in the Assistant pane and
    "nothing else happens". Root cause: the only formatter between the dispatched structured result and the chat
    message, `formatEventOutputMarkdown`, understands ONLY the summarize schema (`tldr`/`summary`/`keywords`); it
    falls into a `tldr===null &amp;&amp; summary===null` branch that renders the object as a ` ```json ` fence. Every
    Compose action returns a different schema (e.g. `compose-explain-clause` → `{explanation, keyConcepts,
    relatedPlaybookIds}`), so all 5 hit the JSON fallback. Separately, `dispatchConsumer` ALSO bridges the terminal
    result onto the `workspace` PaneEventBus channel as section events, which in Compose is the editor (no section
    renderer subscribed) → the "nothing else happens" half. Fix: a Compose-aware, per-action PROSE formatter keyed
    on the action id / bindingId; keep the JSON fence only as a genuine last-resort for unknown shapes.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Frontend engineer fluent in the Compose dispatch→chat seam (`dispatchComposeAction` → `dispatchConsumer` →
    `formatEventOutputMarkdown` → `makeLocalAssistantMessage`) and the 5 Compose action output schemas. You add a
    grounded prose formatter that never paraphrases beyond the returned fields.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Each of the 5 Compose actions renders its structured result as readable prose in the Assistant: e.g.
    explain-clause → the `explanation` paragraph + a "Key concepts" list (+ related-playbook refs if present);
    compare-to-playbook / draft-alternative / summarize-word-changes / defined-terms mapped to their own field
    shapes. The generic ` ```json ` fence appears ONLY for a genuinely unrecognized shape. The stray
    `workspace`-channel section bridge in the Compose surface no longer produces dead/duplicate output (suppressed
    or routed to the intended sink, e.g. the task-072 Q&A highlight), so a click yields exactly one coherent
    Assistant response.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Path: `ComposeAiToolbar.handleActionClick` (`ComposeAiToolbar.tsx:463-465`) → composeActionBridge →
      `ConversationPane.dispatchComposeAction` (`ConversationPane.tsx:196-207`) → `dispatchConsumer`
      (`dispatchConsumer.ts:383-612`, returns `.result`) → `formatEventOutputMarkdown(dispatched.result)`
      (`DocumentUploadedEventStream.ts:218-232`) → `makeLocalAssistantMessage` (`summarizeRouting.ts:172-179`,
      tags `responseType:"markdown"`). Workspace-channel bridge: `dispatchConsumer.ts:487-527`
      (`section_started`/`section_completed`). Output schemas: `infra/dataverse/outputschemas/compose-*.schema.json`
      (explain-clause, compare-to-playbook, draft-alternative, summarize-word-changes, defined-terms).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="dispatch-to-chat-injection" edit="true">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (dispatchComposeAction ~196-207)</file>
      <file purpose="result-formatter" edit="true">the formatter that owns formatEventOutputMarkdown (DocumentUploadedEventStream.ts ~218-232) and/or a new compose-result-format module co-located with summarizeRouting.ts</file>
      <file purpose="workspace-channel-bridge" edit="maybe">dispatchConsumer.ts ~487-527 (decide the Compose-surface destination for section events; suppress or route to 072 QA)</file>
      <file purpose="output-schemas" edit="false">infra/dataverse/outputschemas/compose-explain-clause.schema.json (+ the other 4)</file>
      <file purpose="local-message-shape" edit="false">summarizeRouting.ts ~172-179 (makeLocalAssistantMessage)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      Key the formatter on the action id / bindingId (available in the ComposeActionRequest), NOT on sniffing
      tldr/summary. Render grounded output only — map the schema's own fields to prose, never invent. Keep the
      JSON fence as a fallback for unknown shapes. For the workspace-channel bridge: in the Compose surface the
      editor has no section renderer, so either suppress those events for compose dispatches or route them to the
      task-072 `compose_qa_highlight`/citation sink — pick the one that yields a single coherent response and
      note the decision.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project (E2E DoD, binding)">NOT ✅ until a REAL-PaneEventBus test drives a Compose action's terminal result (e.g. an explain-clause `{explanation, keyConcepts}` payload) through `dispatchComposeAction` and asserts the injected Assistant message is PROSE (contains the explanation text + key-concepts), NOT a ```json code block. A shape-only unit test on the formatter alone is insufficient — it must go through the injection seam.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Grounded output only — the formatter maps returned fields; it must not paraphrase or add content beyond the payload (matches the "render verbatim, never paraphrased" intent of the current fallback).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Keep the JSON fence as the last-resort branch for genuinely unknown shapes (do not delete it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">PaneEventBus usage stays within the established contract; if suppressing/rerouting the workspace-channel bridge, do it at the Compose-surface boundary, not by mutating the shared dispatchConsumer contract for other surfaces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Markdown/prose renders within the existing chat message renderer; no new hard-coded styling.</constraint>
  </constraints>

