  <justification component="Compose-aware result formatter (extends formatEventOutputMarkdown)">
    <existing>`formatEventOutputMarkdown` + `makeLocalAssistantMessage` already own the dispatched-result→chat rendering; it handles the summarize schema.</existing>
    <extension>Extend the same formatter (branch by action id) to the 5 Compose schemas; keep the generic JSON fence as fallback. No new rendering pipeline.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, every inline AI action shows an unreadable JSON blob — the actions "work" on the wire but are unusable, exactly the owner's UAT experience.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the triage note + tasks 046/072 + the 5 output schemas. Read the dispatch→chat path and confirm the tldr/summary fallback branch + the workspace-channel bridge.</step>
    <step order="1">Add a per-action prose formatter (keyed on action id/bindingId) mapping each of the 5 Compose output schemas to grounded markdown; wire it into `dispatchComposeAction`'s injection (or into `formatEventOutputMarkdown` with an action-id branch). Keep the JSON fence as last resort.</step>
    <step order="2">Resolve the workspace-channel bridge for the Compose surface (suppress for compose dispatches or route to the 072 QA highlight) so a click yields exactly one coherent Assistant response; document the decision.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a real-PaneEventBus test: feed an explain-clause `{explanation, keyConcepts}` terminal result through `dispatchComposeAction` and assert the injected message is prose (explanation + key concepts), not ```json; add at least one more action shape (e.g. defined-terms) and an unknown-shape case asserting the fallback still fences.</step>
    <step order="4">Recompile the affected packages per code-page-deploy cache rules; run the bus/component tests + lint.</step>
    <step order="5">code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</output>
