    <output type="test">real-PaneEventBus test: Compose action result → prose Assistant message (per-action + unknown-shape fallback)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">(E2E, non-waivable) A real-PaneEventBus test drives an explain-clause terminal result through `dispatchComposeAction` and asserts the injected Assistant message is PROSE (explanation + key concepts), not a ```json fence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">At least 2 of the 5 action schemas are covered by tests; each renders grounded prose from its own fields.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(negative) A genuinely unknown result shape still renders via the JSON fence fallback (branch preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A single inline-AI click yields exactly one coherent Assistant response — the workspace-channel section bridge no longer produces dead/duplicate output in the Compose surface.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The formatter adds no content beyond the returned payload fields (grounded).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

